  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1245 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nThe subtropical ridge will continue its slow transition to the\neast eventually settling over the northern Gulf coast. This will \nlead to stronger subsidence and less convection in the long term. \nIt will also likely produce temperatures a few degrees higher in \nthe middle of the week. The NBM has been consistently forecasting \nhigher dewpoints over the Coastal Plains in the long term and if \nthis verifies it will mean Heat Advisory heat indices. However, \nthe trend has been for the dewpoint forecast to come in lower as \nit moves into the short term. We'll have to see if this continues.",
